To add links to every post on your website, you'll need to make modifications to your existing configuration. Here's a revised version that includes adding a unique link to each post:

**Assumptions:**

1. You have a directory structure for your blog posts, with each post in its own subdirectory (e.g., `posts/2023/01/post-1/`).
2. Each post has an `index.html` file with the post's content.
3. You want to add a link to each post on your website, with the link text being the post's title.

**Revised configuration:**
```nginx
server {
    listen 443 ssl http2;
    listen [::]:443 ssl http2;
    server_name www.askfundu.com;
    root /usr/share/nginx/html;

    # ... existing configuration ...

    location / {
        root /usr/share/nginx/html;
        index index.html index.htm;
        try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html;

        # Add links to each post
        location ~ ^/posts/[0-9]{4}/[0-9]{2}/([a-zA-Z0-9-]+)\/$ {
            set $post_title $1;
            {
                index /posts/$1/index.html;
                extralibc </path/to/templates/post-link.html>;
            }
        }
    }
}
```
**New directives:**

1. `location ~ ^/posts/[0-9]{4}/[0-9]{2}/([a-zA-Z0-9-]+)\/$` matches URLs that start with `/posts/` followed by a 4-digit year, 2-digit month, and the post's title.
2. `set $post_title $1` retrieves the post's title from the matched URL.
3. `index /posts/$1/index.html` sets the `index` directive to point to the post's HTML file.
4. `extralicb </path/to/templates/post-link.html>` includes a template to generate the link to each post. You'll need to create this template file (e.g., `post-link.html`) in the specified directory.

**Example post-link.html template:**
```html
<a href="/posts/{{$post_title}}/">{{ $post_title }}</a>
```
This template uses the `$post_title` variable to display the post's title as a link to the post's HTML file.

**How it works:**

1. When a user visits your website, Nginx serves the default `index.html` file.
2. If the URL matches the `location ~ ^/posts/...` pattern, Nginx sets the `post_title` variable and includes the `post-link.html` template to generate the link.
3. The link's href attribute is set to the URL of the post's HTML file (e.g., `/posts/2023/01/post-1/index.html`).

